# mythology.kb — the myths, epics and folklore traditions of the world.
#
# `philosophy.kb` describes the living religions as institutions, carefully and from outside.
# This file is the neighbouring subject: the *stories* — Greek, Norse, Egyptian, Hindu, Chinese —
# which general knowledge treats as literature and history rather than as doctrine, and which the
# corpus held nothing of. "Who is Zeus", "what is the Ramayana about", "what is a phoenix" are
# ordinary quiz questions and every one of them came back empty.
#
# **Everything here is written as what a tradition tells, never as what is the case.** A figure is
# `is_a=Greek god` — a role inside a story — and never `is_a=god`, and no line asserts that any
# being exists or acted. That is the same restraint `philosophy.kb` applies to living religion,
# and it is what lets a fact store hold this material honestly: "the Iliad says Achilles was
# nearly invulnerable" is a fact about a poem, and the poem is the subject.

# --- what a myth is ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
mythology | is_a=body of stories | means=the traditional stories a culture tells about its gods, origins and heroes | purpose=explaining the world and carrying a people's values | has_kind=Greek mythology | has_kind=Norse mythology | has_kind=Egyptian mythology | has_kind=Hindu mythology
myth | is_a=story | means=a traditional story involving beings and events outside ordinary experience | has_property=told as significant rather than as reportage
legend | is_a=story | means=a traditional story attached to a real place or person | has_property=treated as having happened, however altered
folklore | is_a=body of stories | means=the tales, songs, sayings and customs passed on within a community | has_property=carried by telling rather than by writing | has_kind=fairy tale | has_kind=fable | has_kind=proverb
fable | is_a=story | means=a short tale, usually with animals, that ends in a moral | has_kind=Aesop's fable | has_kind=Panchatantra tale
fairy tale | is_a=story | means=a folk tale with enchantment in it, usually told to children
proverb | is_a=saying | means=a short traditional saying that states a general truth
creation myth | is_a=myth | means=a story of how the world came to be | has_property=nearly every culture has one
flood myth | is_a=myth | means=a story of a great flood that destroys and renews the world | has_property=found independently in many traditions
hero | is_a=role in a story | means=a figure who undertakes something beyond ordinary human capacity | involves=a trial | involves=a return
quest | is_a=element of a story | means=a journey undertaken to obtain or achieve something
oracle | is_a=element of a story | means=a source that gives ambiguous knowledge of the future | causes=a prophecy that is fulfilled in an unexpected way
prophecy | is_a=element of a story | means=a statement of what is to come | causes=characters acting to avoid it and bringing it about
pantheon | is_a=group | means=the whole set of figures a mythology recognises
epic poem as a form | is_a=poem | means=a long narrative poem about heroic deeds | has_property=usually composed to be recited aloud

# --- Greek and Roman ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
Greek mythology | is_a=mythology | located_in=Ancient Greece | has_part=Olympian gods | involves=the Trojan War | causes=much of the vocabulary of European art and literature
Olympian gods | is_a=pantheon | part_of=Greek mythology | located_in=Mount Olympus | has_kind=Zeus | has_kind=Hera | has_kind=Poseidon | has_kind=Athena | has_kind=Apollo
Zeus | is_a=Greek god | involves=the sky and thunder | has_property=the chief of the Olympian gods
Hera | is_a=Greek god | involves=marriage | has_property=the consort of Zeus in the stories
Poseidon | is_a=Greek god | involves=the sea and earthquakes
Athena | is_a=Greek god | involves=wisdom and skilled craft | located_in=Athens as its patron in the stories
Apollo | is_a=Greek god | involves=light, music, poetry and prophecy
Artemis | is_a=Greek god | involves=the hunt and the Moon
Ares | is_a=Greek god | involves=war
Aphrodite | is_a=Greek god | involves=love and beauty
Hermes | is_a=Greek god | involves=messages, travellers and trade
Hades | is_a=Greek god | involves=the underworld
Demeter | is_a=Greek god | involves=grain and the harvest | involves=the story that explains the seasons
Hephaestus | is_a=Greek god | involves=fire and metalworking
Prometheus | is_a=figure in Greek mythology | involves=bringing fire to humanity | involves=being punished for it
Pandora | is_a=figure in Greek mythology | involves=a jar whose opening released every trouble into the world
Heracles | is_a=Greek hero | involves=twelve labours | also_known_as=Hercules
Achilles | is_a=Greek hero | part_of=the Iliad | has_property=vulnerable only at the heel in the later stories
Odysseus | is_a=Greek hero | part_of=the Odyssey | involves=a ten year journey home | has_property=known in the stories for cunning rather than strength
Perseus | is_a=Greek hero | involves=the killing of Medusa
Theseus | is_a=Greek hero | involves=the labyrinth and the Minotaur
Icarus | is_a=figure in Greek mythology | involves=wings of wax | involves=flying too near the Sun
Midas | is_a=figure in Greek mythology | involves=a touch that turned everything to gold
Sisyphus | is_a=figure in Greek mythology | involves=rolling a boulder uphill for ever
Narcissus | is_a=figure in Greek mythology | involves=falling in love with his own reflection
Trojan War | is_a=legend | part_of=Greek mythology | involves=the siege of Troy | involves=the wooden horse
Trojan horse | is_a=element of a story | part_of=Trojan War | means=a hollow horse concealing soldiers | causes=the word for a deception that is welcomed in
Medusa | is_a=creature in Greek mythology | has_property=snakes for hair | has_property=a gaze that turned onlookers to stone
Minotaur | is_a=creature in Greek mythology | has_property=the head of a bull on a human body | located_in=the labyrinth
Pegasus | is_a=creature in Greek mythology | has_property=a winged horse
Cyclops | is_a=creature in Greek mythology | has_property=a single eye
Sphinx | is_a=creature in mythology | involves=a riddle | located_in=Greek and Egyptian traditions alike
Roman mythology | is_a=mythology | located_in=Ancient Rome | has_property=largely the Greek stories under Roman names | involves=the founding of Rome
Jupiter as a god | is_a=Roman god | involves=the sky and thunder | has_property=the Roman counterpart of Zeus
Mars as a god | is_a=Roman god | involves=war
Venus as a goddess | is_a=Roman god | involves=love and beauty
Romulus and Remus | is_a=legend | part_of=Roman mythology | involves=twins raised by a wolf | involves=the founding of Rome

# --- Norse and Egyptian --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
Norse mythology | is_a=mythology | located_in=Scandinavia | has_part=Asgard | involves=Ragnarok | causes=the English names of four days of the week
Asgard | is_a=place in a myth | part_of=Norse mythology | means=the home of the Norse gods
Odin | is_a=Norse god | involves=wisdom, poetry and war | has_property=gave an eye for knowledge in the stories
Thor | is_a=Norse god | involves=thunder | has_part=Mjolnir
Mjolnir | is_a=object in a myth | part_of=Norse mythology | means=Thor's hammer
Loki | is_a=Norse god | involves=trickery and shape changing
Freya | is_a=Norse god | involves=love, beauty and war
Valhalla | is_a=place in a myth | part_of=Norse mythology | means=the hall where those who fell in battle are received
Yggdrasil | is_a=element of a story | part_of=Norse mythology | means=the world tree joining the realms
Ragnarok | is_a=myth | part_of=Norse mythology | means=the foretold battle in which the world ends and is renewed
Valkyrie | is_a=figure in Norse mythology | involves=choosing who falls in battle
Egyptian mythology | is_a=mythology | located_in=Ancient Egypt | involves=the afterlife | involves=the Nile
Ra | is_a=Egyptian god | involves=the Sun | has_property=chief among the gods in much of the tradition
Osiris | is_a=Egyptian god | involves=the afterlife and rebirth
Isis | is_a=Egyptian god | involves=magic and healing
Anubis | is_a=Egyptian god | involves=embalming and the guidance of the dead | has_property=depicted with a jackal's head
Horus | is_a=Egyptian god | involves=kingship and the sky | has_property=depicted with a falcon's head
mummification | is_a=practice | located_in=Ancient Egypt | purpose=preserving a body for the afterlife | requires=removal of moisture
Book of the Dead | is_a=text | located_in=Ancient Egypt | purpose=guiding the dead through the afterlife

